| Type of Tools and Equipment | Description |
|-----------------------------|-------------|
| Mobile Device Management (MDM) software | Enterprise software (e.g. Microsoft Intune, VMware Workspace ONE, Jamf) used to remotely configure, monitor, and secure mobile devices at scale. MDM pushes Wi-Fi profiles, email settings, VPN configurations, security policies (encryption, screen lock, remote wipe), and app installations to enrolled devices. Essential for organisations managing more than a handful of mobile devices. |
| SIM ejector tool and SIM cards | The SIM ejector tool opens the SIM tray on smartphones and tablets. SIM cards (nano, micro, or eSIM) provide cellular connectivity. During configuration, insert the correct SIM and verify cellular data connectivity, carrier settings, and APN configuration. For eSIM, scan the carrier QR code or enter the activation details. |
| USB cable and charging adapter | Used to connect the mobile device to a computer for initial setup, data transfer, firmware update, or charging. USB-C is standard on most modern devices; Lightning is used on older iPhones. Ensure the cable supports data transfer, not charge-only. |
| Wi-Fi network access | Required during initial setup to download updates, enrol in MDM, install apps, and configure cloud accounts. The technician must have the SSID, security key, and any certificate or 802.1X credentials needed to connect the device to the corporate Wi-Fi. |
| Backup and restore tools | Built-in tools (e.g. Google Backup, iCloud, Samsung Smart Switch) or third-party software used to back up user data before troubleshooting and to restore data onto replacement devices. Backup includes contacts, photos, app data, messages, and settings. Verify backup completeness before performing a factory reset or device swap. |
| Diagnostic and testing apps | Tools used to verify device functionality after configuration: Wi-Fi analyser (signal strength and channel), speed test (bandwidth verification), email test (send/receive), VPN connection test, and GPS accuracy test. These confirm the device meets the job order requirements before commissioning. |


