| Common Fault During Mobile Configuration | Cause | Action |
|-------------------------------------------|-------|--------|
| Wi-Fi connects but no internet access | Wrong security key, DHCP scope exhausted, MAC filtering blocking device, or proxy misconfigured | Verify SSID and security key; check DHCP server lease pool; add device MAC to allowed list if filtering is enabled; check proxy settings in Wi-Fi advanced options |
| Email fails to sync (authentication error) | Wrong server address or port, incorrect credentials, security certificate not trusted, or two-factor authentication not configured | Verify server settings against the job order specification; re-enter credentials; install required security certificate; configure app-specific password if 2FA is enabled |
| VPN connection fails | VPN profile incorrect, server address wrong, certificate expired or missing, or firewall blocking VPN port | Verify VPN configuration (server, protocol, port); reinstall VPN certificate; check with network team if VPN server is reachable; try alternative VPN protocol if available |
| App installation fails (incompatible) | Device OS version too old, insufficient storage, app requires higher RAM, or app not available in region | Check app minimum requirements against device specification; update device OS if possible; free storage space; download app from alternative source if region-restricted |
| Device not enrolling in MDM | Enrolment URL or QR code expired, device OS not supported by MDM, or network blocking MDM server | Verify enrolment link is current; check device OS version against MDM requirements; connect to a network that allows access to the MDM server; contact MDM administrator |
| Battery drains rapidly after configuration | Background sync too frequent, GPS always on, screen brightness too high, or rogue app consuming resources | Adjust email sync frequency; set GPS to battery-saving mode; enable auto-brightness; check battery usage in settings to identify the draining app; uninstall or restrict it |


