## Attitude, Safety and Environmental

### Workplace Safety
- **Lithium Battery Safety:** Handle mobile device batteries with care; do not puncture, bend, or expose them to excessive heat. A swollen or damaged lithium battery poses fire and chemical burn risks -- discontinue use immediately, place the device on a non-flammable surface, and follow organisational hazardous material procedures for disposal. Never attempt to pry open a swollen battery.
- **Screen and Glass Handling:** Mobile device screens are made of fragile glass that can crack or shatter during repair or configuration. Wear safety glasses when working with cracked screens and handle broken devices with gloves to avoid cuts. Dispose of broken screen glass in a designated sharps or e-waste container.
- **Data Privacy and Security:** Perform a complete data wipe (factory reset) before redeploying or disposing of any mobile device to protect personal and corporate data. Verify the wipe is complete by checking that no user accounts, files, or cached data remain. Follow the organisation's data protection policy (e.g. PDPA) when handling devices that contain personal information.
- **Ergonomic Device Testing:** Maintain a neutral wrist and neck posture when testing and configuring mobile devices for extended periods. Use a device stand or holder at eye level to reduce repetitive strain. Take regular breaks during batch provisioning sessions to prevent fatigue-related errors and musculoskeletal discomfort.

### Environmental Considerations
- **E-waste Management:** Properly dispose of defective hardware components, circuit boards, and packaging materials through authorised e-waste recycling centres. Never dispose of electronics in regular trash or landfill.
- **Energy Efficiency:** Configure systems to use power-saving modes and efficient power supplies. Avoid unnecessary idle time and follow organisational energy conservation policies.

### Professional Attitudes
- **Punctuality and Reliability:** Complete mobile device configuration work on schedule to meet user handover deadlines and support business operations.
- **Integrity in Documentation:** Prepare accurate and complete commissioning reports with all hardware details, software versions, and test results. Honest documentation supports future troubleshooting and maintains system integrity.
- **Teamwork and Support:** Collaborate with help desk staff and other technicians; share knowledge about system configurations and troubleshooting techniques to improve overall technical capability.
- **Attention to Detail:** Verify every connection, configuration setting, and test result to ensure mobile device configuration tasks are completed correctly and devices function as intended.

